          <p>
            Renting deserves more consideration than it gets. If your only heavy job is a driveway once a year, two days of rental cost less than a gas machine and you skip the fuel, oil and storage entirely. Owning starts to make sense around three or more substantial jobs per year, or when you have several different surfaces to keep on top of through the season.
          </p>

          <p>
            Pressure washing is often step one of a bigger project. A clean, dry deck is ready for stain, and concrete that has been washed and allowed to dry is ready for sealer. If that is your plan, look at our <a href="/best-deck-stain-reviews/">deck stain rankings</a> and <a href="/best-concrete-sealer/">concrete sealer picks</a>, and budget the coating with the machine. And if the job is just getting a driveway clean, start with the right chemistry from our <a href="/best-driveway-cleaner/">driveway cleaner guide</a> before you reach for more pressure.
